{"name":"Grape Shake","hex":"#886971","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, round, smooth-skinned edible fruit, usually purple, red, or green, that grows in bunches on female vines of most species of genus Vitis and the self-fertile plants of species Vitis vinifera.","Any woody vine of genus Vitis that bears clusters of grapes; a grapevine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing grapes or having a grape flavor.","Of a dark purplish red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grape"},{"term":"shake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (something) to move rapidly in opposite directions alternatingly.","To move (one's head) from side to side, especially to indicate refusal, reluctance, or disapproval."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of shaking or being shaken; tremulous or back-and-forth motion.","A twitch, a spasm, a tremor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grape","blocks":[{"text":"A grape is a fruit, botanically a berry, of the deciduous woody vines of the flowering plant genus Vitis. Grapes are a non-climacteric type of fruit, generally occurring in clusters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grape","wikidata":"Q10978"},{"title":"Shades of violet","blocks":[{"text":"Violet is a color term derived from the flower of the same name. There are numerous variations of the color violet, a sampling of which are shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Color_icon_violet_v3.svg/330px-Color_icon_violet_v3.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_viole